      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_157"
      ],
      "explanation": "The basic properties of algebraic fractions only allow multiplying (or dividing) both the numerator and denominator by the same nonzero polynomial expression; adding the same expression is not allowed. Since \\(m\\) may be 0, C is incorrect. Since \\(y-x=-(x-y)\\), we have \\((x-y)/(y-x)=-1\\).",
